{
  "run_id": "PMC12716175__problem_constrained__pcd_D_o3mini__s1",
  "auditor": "trapi:gpt-5.6-sol_2026-07-09",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The starting material consists of W particles or interconnected W ligaments embedded in a Cu matrix.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The untreated W–Cu composite exhibits phase separation and interfacial void formation under heat-transfer and irradiation service conditions.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "An effective intervention is addition of 0.5–2 wt% Ti before consolidation.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Controlled added carbon or residual carbon on W surfaces can supply the carbon needed for the intervention.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sintering near 1200°C under an Ar/H2 atmosphere can produce the intended interfacial structure.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed processing will form a uniformly distributed nanoscale TiC interphase at W–Cu interfaces.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514646::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "During sintering, Ti reacts with available carbon to form a carbide.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514646::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The carbide formed at W surfaces will specifically be TiC.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514646::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "A TiC interlayer chemically bonds with both W and Cu.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Ti-containing carbide interphase improves interfacial adhesion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514646::web::003::1_introduction",
        "PMC7514646::web::014::4_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed interphase reduces interfacial energy.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514646::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Improved interfacial bonding reduces the driving force for W–Cu phase separation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Carbide formation can reduce interfacial cracks or microvoids.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514646::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The TiC interphase suppresses void nucleation during thermal cycling and irradiation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Ti-modified W–Cu composite will have higher thermal conductivity than the untreated composite.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified interface will remain void-resistant under high temperature gradients and irradiation relevant to W-based plasma-facing material/Cu-based cooling-component joints.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Excessive or coarse TiC growth can detrimentally impede thermal conduction.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Applicability is limited to service conditions under which the nanoscale TiC interlayer remains chemically and structurally stable.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The optimal Ti and carbon levels and sintering profile are not yet known and require experimental determination.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    }
